  "body": "It is rare to find a home that delivers so completely. Beautifully renovated, filled with light and enjoying panoramic views, this is a phenomenal family home where luxury feels relaxed and every member of the family, especially teenagers, have a space of their own. \r\n\r\nSet on 916sqm of freehold land, the home offers approximately 450sqm of living over three generous levels, connected by an internal lift. There are inviting spaces to gather, quiet rooms in which to retreat, a pool for long summer afternoons, a gym and steam sauna, a putting green and superb outdoor entertaining. Whether the house is full of family or your children's besties, this home will be the hub for weekend sleep overs and family milestones from sweet sixteens to twenty firsts. \r\n\r\nAlthough the address is St Heliers Bay Road, the home is conveniently accessed from Glen Atkinson Street and faces north, away from the road. Its elevated position and double-glazed joinery make it genuinely quiet and private, with wonderful sun and expansive views creating an immediate sense of calm.\r\n\r\nThe middle level is the heart of the home. A gorgeous designer kitchen and scullery anchor the open-plan living and dining areas, which flow naturally to a covered deck with an outdoor kitchen. It is a wonderful setting for everything from morning coffee in the sun to large family gatherings and relaxed summer evenings. A dedicated study could double as cosy TV room for older children. \r\n\r\nA separate lodge-style lounge with a fireplace provides a warm and inviting retreat. It is the perfect room to settle into at the end of the day, while a powder room and generous shared office complete this level.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the master suite is a true sanctuary, with a large walk-in wardrobe, luxurious ensuite and spectacular sunset views. Three further bedrooms and a family bathroom provide plenty of room for children, each with their own sense of space and privacy.\r\n\r\nThe ground floor creates yet another zone to enjoy. A fifth bedroom and bathroom are ideal for older children, guests or extended family, while the third living area, gym and bespoke steam sauna make this level feel like a private wellness retreat. A wine cellar, full laundry, extensive storage and double internal-access garaging ensure the practical side of family life is equally well catered for.\r\n\r\nOutside, the beautifully landscaped grounds continue the resort-like feeling. The private heated saltwater pool sits among the palms, while the putting green adds another relaxed space for family and friends to enjoy. It feels private, peaceful and wonderfully removed from the pace of everyday life.\r\n\r\nThe home has been comprehensively renovated with quality and longevity in mind, including a new roof, double-glazed joinery and vertical shiplap weatherboard cladding. The styling is sophisticated without feeling formal, creating a home that is impressive from the moment you arrive yet comfortable enough to enjoy every day.\r\n\r\nThe scale and separation make it exceptional for families, while couples will appreciate having plenty of room for teenage children, grandchildren and friends to stay without compromising their own privacy.\r\n\r\nOnly minutes from St Heliers and Kohimarama beaches, cafes and village life, this is coastal living on an extraordinary scale. St Heliers offers considerably more for your money than many of Auckland's other premium suburbs, and few homes bring together this level of space, quality, privacy and lifestyle so completely.\r\n\r\nMore than simply a beautiful house, this is a home where everyone has their own space, family and friends naturally come together, and everyday life feels very special.\r\n\r\nAuction: 11:00am, Wednesday 21 October 2026 (Unless Sold Prior)\r\nKeywords: Kohimarama, Mission Bay , Glendowie, Selwyn College, St Thomas's Primary, Remuera, Parnell, Westmere, Herne Bay, Ponsonby, St Kentigerns, Baradene, Sacred Heart College.",
